From: local
Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: use direct platform audio sink for MediaStream

The WebAudio provider wrapper can silently build a partial audio bin when an
element factory is unavailable at runtime. In that state the tee is present but
the actual sink branch is absent, leaving playbin pending PLAYING while the
MediaStream appsrc queue fills.

MediaStream playback does not need the WebAudio capture tee for normal remote
audio output. Route it directly to the platform sink by default. Keep
WEBKIT_GST_MEDIASTREAM_DIRECT_AUDIO_SINK=0 as a rollback switch.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@
 #if ENABLE(WEB_AUDIO)
+    const char* directMediaStreamAudio = g_getenv("WEBKIT_GST_MEDIASTREAM_DIRECT_AUDIO_SINK");
+    if (isMediaStreamPlayer() && (!directMediaStreamAudio || g_strcmp0(directMediaStreamAudio, "0"))) {
+        GST_WARNING_OBJECT(pipeline(), "Using direct platform audio sink for MediaStream playback");
+        return audioSink;
+    }
+
     GstElement* audioSinkBin = gst_bin_new("audio-sink");
     ensureAudioSourceProvider();
     m_audioSourceProvider->configureAudioBin(audioSinkBin, audioSink);
